{
  "id": "iteration-2-retro-cascade",
  "name": "Day-7 reversal cascade - interest reversed and re-credited twice, fees permanent",
  "description": "An 8-day window with capitalization still on day 6. A 2000 AED debit back-dated into day 3 arrives on day 7, after interest has already been credited: four overdraft fees are raised, the old interest credit is reversed and a smaller one posted. Day 8 reverses the debit and interest is restated upwards again - but the four fees do not reverse with it, so the account settles 100 AED below where it would have closed had the debit never arrived.",
